CLR: per-gate logging for the retained-PM4 graph path, and DEBUG_HIP_GRAPH_PM4_SPLIT.

Applies with -p1 at projects/clr of rocm-10-sdk-pm4-prepared-source (Codex's PM4 SDK port).
Source of truth: /mnt/Home/src/pm4-clr-gatelog/rocm-10-sdk-pm4-prepared-source, 7f6a76f..7e5850b.

1. rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp, CreateGraphPm4Batch: one "[hipGraph][PM4-WHY]" line per
   rejected batch naming the gate (extension-unavailable, single-packet, size-mismatch, profiling,
   capabilities, non-kernel-packet, completion-signal, kernel-not-in-map, rocr-create-failed).
2. DEBUG_HIP_GRAPH_PM4_SPLIT (flags.hpp, default true; only consulted when DEBUG_HIP_GRAPH_PM4 is
   on). In hip_graph_internal.cpp/.hpp, leading non-kernel packets (the segment's cross-stream
   barrier-AND waits) and a trailing completion-signalled kernel go out as AQL, and the kernel run
   between them is retained as PM4. Without it a multi-packet batch that starts with a barrier-AND
   fails the "every packet is a kernel dispatch" gate and nothing is retained.

